{"clock":1,"nonce":"7e87b5a9dccbb9d8f94151b322015674","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792322502,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5908987041"},"data":{"body":"Milestone M4 of the work-unit PRD (`docs/prd/work-unit.md`): review a branch's changes in the issue (a Changes tab), and mirror review comments with the GitHub PR. M1 (numbers), M2 (roles) and M3 (the PR gate) are merged on main 2b26234. M4 is planned only: nothing is built yet, and its fork changes are agreed with the main session.\n\n**Order:** fix the findings of the review issue \"Fix the 2026-10-17 review\" (86349c0) on the fork first. Its fixes and M4's fork part both change `bridge/core/syncpush.go` (pushChanges, planPush).\n\n\nOpen Claude Code in `~/works/git/github/git-board` and paste everything below the line. It was written by the M3 session that built the gate, and the \"memory file m4-bridge-agreement.md\" it mentions is that session's memory for this repository. The agreement is repeated in full below.\n\n---\n\nContinue the \"work unit\" PRD for git-board: build milestone M4 (review in git-board). M1 (numbers), M2 (roles) and M3 (the PR gate) are done and merged.\n\n- docs/prd/work-unit.md: the PRD and the spec. Read the \"Decisions\" table, \"M4\", the M3 notes (\"Built 2026-10-17\", \"Live test\"), \"The six questions\", \"Out of scope\", \"Open, not blocking\" and \"Constraints\".\n- docs/configuration.md § Branches: the Development section and its PR gate, which M4 sits on.\n- docs/prd/work-unit-m3-plan.md: the plan style that worked.\n- Your memory file m4-bridge-agreement.md (in MEMORY.md): the git-bug fork changes already agreed with the main session. Don't re-ask them.\n\n- M3 is merged: git-board main 2b26234 (prd/gate after numbers-ui). Start M4's git-board work from the current origin/main (2b26234 or later).\n- M3 gives you:\n  - internal/ghpr: Client{API, Token}; Find(repo, branch) finds a PR by head ref; Required(repo, base); Open; Merge(sha); Gate().\n  - Backend.GitHubToken(): the keyring token whose login is the identity's GitHub login.\n  - Backend.GitHubRepo(\"origin\").\n  - Routes: GET/POST /api/issues/{id}/pulls and POST /api/issues/{id}/pulls/{n}/merge.\n  - web/src/gate.ts: tested helpers.\n  - IssueBranches.vue: layout B.\n- git-bug's tokens have the `repo` scope only. Any GraphQL field that needs read:org (a team's fields) fails the whole query. Verify GitHub queries with the keyring token, never with `gh`'s token, which has more scopes and hid this in M3.\n\n- `review:*` keys on AddComment ops:\n  - a line comment: review:path, review:line, review:side (old|new), review:commit, review:pr (github.com/o/r#26);\n  - a reply: the same anchor plus review:reply-to;\n  - a review: review:state (APPROVE|REQUEST_CHANGES|COMMENT), review:commit, review:pr.\n  - Resolving is a SetMetadata review:resolved. The last SetMetadata wins.\n- An imported PR comment's origin is `sync:github.com/o/r:pr-comment`, never ending in `:id`.\n- Import: an optional SyncOptions callback `PullsOf(bug entity.Id) []string`, GitHub only; nil means no PR import. The CLI then imports no PR comments; document that.\n- Export: the op's review:pr names the PR.\n  - In pushChanges, an op with any review:* key or a pr-comment origin is never posted as an issue comment, on any remote. It goes to the PR on GitHub instead.\n  - The same skip goes in planPush (dry run) and in the EditComment loop.\n- You build it, in a worktree of ~/works/git/github/git-bug on a branch off bridge-sync (e.g. review-sync). Engine tests with the synctest fake come first.\n- Before handing it over, run gofmt (Go 1.26) and `make generate` (doc/md) locally. Upstream CI runs only on the fork's PR #1.\n- The main session reviews it, merges it into bridge-sync, tags the fork and bumps git-board's pin, after the user's OK. Until the pin bumps, git-board's M4 code can build against the fork only through a local `replace`, which is never committed. Order: fork first, then the pin, then git-board's M4 code on top.\n\n- Layout A: a \"Changes\" tab beside Conversation and History on the issue page. The gate stays in the side panel's Development section.\n- The diff is computed locally, from the merge base of dev and the branch to its head. A commit picker shows one commit, or what changed since your last review.\n- Large diffs: the file list comes first (`git diff --numstat`), and each file's diff loads when opened. Three groups:\n  - To review: files under 1,000 lines open by themselves.\n  - Large: over 3,000 lines, folded, with \"Load the first 5,000\" and a copyable `git diff dev...\u003cbranch\u003e -- \u003cpath\u003e`.\n  - Generated: `linguist-generated` in .gitattributes (`git check-attr`), folded and left out of the \"viewed\" count.\n- \"Viewed\" is per viewer, kept in the browser.\n- Releases are out of scope (worktree git-board-release).\n\n- M4's Done-when needs \"an approval made in git-board satisfies the code-owner rule\". GitHub refuses an approval from the PR's author, so it needs a second GitHub account.\n- It also needs a ruleset with a code-owner review on guilbep/git-board-test. That repository is private on a free plan, so rulesets aren't enforced; M3's live test ran without one.\n- Ask which account, and whether to make the repo public or confirm Pro. Ask before each write to a scratch forge.\n\n- NEVER push to co2-calculator or to any EPFL-ENAC repository. Nothing goes to a remote unless the user asks for that action.\n- Live tests only on the scratch forges: guilbep/git-board-test, guilbep/git-bug-sync-test, gitlab.epfl.ch project 42400, GitHub Project #1. Prefer local bare remotes and fakes in tests.\n- The fork has one branch and one PR (bridge-sync). Never push bridge-sync or tags. Don't open the upstream PR, and don't comment on git-bug#1476.\n- The main session (git-bug-95) merges and pushes git-board branches after the user's OK. Hand it a branch; don't merge yourself.\n\n1. Make a worktree: `~/works/git/github/git-board-review` on branch `prd/review`, from origin/main. Make the fork worktree as above.\n2. Use the brainstorming skill briefly: the PRD is the spec, so ask only the open question above. Then write a plan at docs/prd/work-unit-m4-plan.md (writing-plans) and execute it inline with TDD (executing-plans, the \"Native\" method), fork part first.\n3. Finish with a fresh reviewer on the most capable model, then one fix pass with a failing-then-passing test per fix.\n4. Before handing over, run: `make ci`, `cd web \u0026\u0026 npm run typecheck \u0026\u0026 npm test`, and gofmt from both Go 1.26 (CI's: `$(GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.0 go env GOROOT)/bin/gofmt -l .`) and Go 1.27. For the fork: gofmt and `make generate`.\n\n- An `rtk` hook rewrites git, grep, curl and go test output. Use `rtk proxy \u003ccmd\u003e`, or a script file, when you need exact output.\n- In zsh, `\"$var:r…\"` is a modifier; write `\"${var}:refs/…\"`.\n- macOS has no `timeout` command; use `go test -timeout`.\n- The web app needs `npm ci` in web/ in a fresh worktree. `npm run build` before `go build` embeds it in git-board-server.\n- git-bug's keyring is one file for every repository, in the user's config directory. Tests store tokens only on gitbugiotest backends (in-memory), or set HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME to a temp dir before gitbugio.Open.\n- Don't run `git bug bridge auth`: it prints token values.\n- The web app is hash-routed: http://localhost:\u003cport\u003e/#/issues/\u003cid\u003e. Navigating to the same hash URL doesn't reload the page; go through about:blank.\n- The Playwright MCP writes `.playwright-mcp/` into the main checkout (~/works/git/github/git-board). Delete it when done.\n- A scratch clone of git-board-test with a configured GitHub sync bridge and an adopted identity is useful for live tests. Set it up in your scratchpad, as M3 did: `git bug pull origin`, `git bug user adopt`, `git bug bridge new --name gh --url https://github.com/guilbep/git-board-test --sync --credential \u003cid\u003e --non-interactive`.","title":"Work unit M4: review in git-board (Changes tab, PR review comments synced)"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792405888,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5908987041"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792405891,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5908987041"},"data":{"add":["kind:feat","prio:p2","status:done"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792405887,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6265167644"},"data":{"body":"Done: landed on main (64d50cd, merge of prd/review), on git-bug fork v0.11.1-sync.6.\n\n- The Changes tab on the issue page: the branch's diff, line comments, replies, reviews (approve, request changes, comment), resolve.\n- Review comments are git-bug comments with review:* metadata; the sync sends them to the pull request their review:pr names, stamped at every sync for the open pull requests on the issue's branches, and brings the pull request's comments and reviews back.\n- Approvals and change requests go only with their author's own token, so they satisfy the code-owner rule.\n- Live test on guilbep/git-board-test PR #28: line comment out, the bot's comment back, the bot's approval read CLEAN under the ruleset, merged from the issue.\n\nLeft as they are: 1714996 (M4 review: known issues)."}}]}